In this paper, we establish a novel connection between the enumerative geometry of topological maps and the structure of generalized non-crossing partitions associated with a finite irreducible Coxeter group~$W$. By encoding minimal reflection factorizations of a Coxeter element $c \in W$ as constellation maps on orientable surfaces, we derive refined generating functions that count factorizations with prescribed block sizes. 

